{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"3d4501e55a6c9b2e7a3ca6e453c59daf56afdbec30e5822899708043526495d5","packTokens":2348,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":2268,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that has the open status and a due date and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response is 200 and contains INV-1\",\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due) when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response does not contain INV-2\",\n    \"Given business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response contains INV-3\",\n    \"Given the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10, today is 2026-10-15, and open invoices are due 2026-10-05 and 2026-10-06 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response contains the invoice due 2026-10-05 and does not contain the invoice due 2026-10-06\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice has any status other than open in the existing invoice data (including paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft or written off) or has no due date, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoices C (paid), D (closed), E (void) and F (draft) are each 30 days past their due date, and open invoice G has no due date when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then none of C, D, E, F or G is in the response\",\n    \"Given invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data when GET the overdue list endpoint is called again with a valid staff token then the response no longer contains INV-6, with no other action needed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders API shall work out overdue status at query time without writing any overdue flag or status to invoice records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue when the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token, with and without filters then every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return, for each overdue invoice, its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given today is 2026-10-15 in the business timezone and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, is due 2026-10-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response's INV-100 entry has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 14\",\n    \"Given today is 2026-09-08, threshold is 7 and open invoice INV-1 is due 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response's INV-1 entry has days overdue 7\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given customer A has 2 overdue invoices and customer B has 3 overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer A then the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices\",\n    \"Given customer C has no overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C then the response is 200 with an empty list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or 91 and over (90+), the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue falls inside that bucket, bounds included.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91 when the overdue list is requested with each bucket in turn then the 7–30 response contains 7 and 30; 31–60 contains 31 and 60; 61–90 contains 61 and 90; 90+ contains only 91\",\n    \"Given customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days and customer B has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days when the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60 then the response contains only customer A's 40-day invoice\",\n    \"Given any data when the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets (e.g. 5-9) then the response is 400 and names the allowed bucket values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to the overdue list endpoint has no valid staff authentication under the existing API's authentication scheme, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and return no invoice or customer data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no authentication credentials and at least one overdue invoice in the database when the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without filters then each response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body\",\n    \"Given an expired or invalid staff token and at least one overdue invoice in the database when the overdue list endpoint is called then the response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing).\",\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing).\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}